```java
String name = request.getParameter("name");
try (PreparedStatement ps =
        con.prepareStatement("SELECT * FROM users WHERE name = ?")) {
    ps.setString(1, name);   // bound as DATA, never as SQL
    try (ResultSet rs = ps.executeQuery()) { /* ... */ }
}
// even ' OR '1'='1 is treated as a literal name string -> no injection
```

*The query is parsed before the value is bound, so input can't alter its structure.*

```java
try (Statement st = con.createStatement()) {
    for (int i = 0; i < 10_000; i++) {
        // the DB parses + plans this SQL 10,000 times
        st.executeUpdate("INSERT INTO logs (msg) VALUES ('row " + i + "')");
    }
}
```

```java
try (PreparedStatement ps =
        con.prepareStatement("INSERT INTO logs (msg) VALUES (?)")) {
    for (int i = 0; i < 10_000; i++) {
        ps.setString(1, "row " + i);
        ps.addBatch();                 // queue
    }
    ps.executeBatch();                 // one round-trip, plan reused
}
```

*Parsed and planned once, parameters rebound each iteration, and batched into far fewer round-trips.*

